Touch geometry, serial packet layout, and serial startup response constants
are adapted from toucca (https://github.com/BlueGlassBlock/toucca), revision adc6b7a,
which is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later. Adaptations separate protocol and state from
the UI, add explicit framing and lifecycle handling, and change serial writing
to a single worker with complete immutable snapshots.

toucca credits: Any2WACCAi by Raymonf; Any2WACCA_with_WACCAVCon by Mishe.W#7250;
WACVR by xiaopeng12138; MaiTouchSensorEmulator by Leapward-Koex.

Brokenithm-iOS by esterTion is the architectural reference for iOS-listener /
Windows-usbmux-client connectivity. No Brokenithm app source or vendored
CocoaAsyncSocket code is included in this implementation.

The MercuryIO 1.0 function ABI, operator-button constants, and led_data layout
are based on the TeamTofuShop's segatools checkout, revision 8a966b2454185699e8b7d256f4ab43384c274ba0
(games/mercuryio and games/mercuryhook). The native adapter and versioned,
bounded shared-memory transport are implemented in Brokencca; segatools itself
is not modified or bundled. See docs/HOOK-IO.md for compatibility scope.

LED-to-cell ordering in ios/Brokencca/BCLed.h is adapted from WACVR by
xiaopeng12138 (https://github.com/xiaopeng12138/WACVR), revision c982169,
Assets/Script/LightManager/LightManager.cs, under GPL-3.0. WACVR and Brokenithm
are references for shared-memory IO; neither project's DLLs are redistributed.

libusbmuxd/iproxy and Apple Mobile Device Support are external dependencies,
not redistributed here. System.IO.Ports is restored via NuGet under its own license.

The Windows capture tools restore Vortice.Direct3D11, Vortice.DXGI, and
Vortice.D3DCompiler 3.6.2 (Amer Koleci and contributors, MIT) and their NuGet
dependencies, plus Microsoft's Windows SDK .NET projections. The capture
implementation is new; toucca remains the window-discovery/calibration reference.
The optional IGraphicsCaptureSession5 ABI signature is checked against Microsoft's
windows-rs Windows/Graphics/Capture metadata. Windows Graphics Capture and
d3dcompiler_47 are system APIs, not separately redistributed DLLs in this source.
